  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>clinical_notes - extracts medications, symptoms, diagnoses and allergies from each clinical note with the
LangExtract service and loads one row per fact.
Needs: the LangExtract service on http://localhost:8765 (qwen2.5:7b) and staging.patient_extractions in the
pgvector kit's genai database.

1. gfn-notes: Get file names, ${Internal.Entry.Current.Directory}/../notes, Regular Expression .*\.txt.
2. load-notes: Load file content in memory, filename from the field filename, UTF-8, the whole file into
   note_text.
3. js-request: Modified JavaScript value: patient_id from short_filename less .txt; request_json with the note,
   the prompt, one worked example with the four classes, model_id ${LX_MODEL}, max_char_buffer 1200,
   extraction_passes 2.
4. rest-extract: REST client, POST http://localhost:8765/extract, body request_json, result response_json.
5. json-extractions: JSON input on response_json: class, text (String), start, end (Integer) from
   $.extractions[*].
6. flt-classes: Filter rows class IN LIST medication;symptom;diagnosis;allergy; TRUE to tbl-extractions, other
   rows dropped.
7. tbl-extractions: Table output on connection genai, staging.patient_extractions: patient_id, class, text,
   start, end.

Parameters: LX_MODEL qwen2.5:7b; PG_HOST localhost, PG_PORT 5433, PG_DATABASE genai, PG_USER
genai, PG_PASSWORD genai.
Shipped data: 5 synthetic notes; 48 facts loaded on the course PC (12, 8, 10, 7 and 11 per patient).</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>630</width>
      <heigth>404</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
